{
  "theory_id": "prompt_vocab_v0",
  "label": "Video prompt vocabulary for the segment prompt editor",
  "checked": "2026-08-18",
  "notes": "Controlled vocabulary of film terms that current text-to-video models respond to. Distilled and re-checked from a 2025-era Japanese prompting guide; terms that stopped working, or that this pipeline overrides anyway, were dropped or marked with caution. Not wired to the UI yet — reference data for chips in the segment prompt editor and for taste-driven STYLE merges. See docs/PROMPTING.md.",
  "layers": [
    {"id": "subject", "role": "who / what is in frame"},
    {"id": "action", "role": "what the subject does inside this clip's seconds"},
    {"id": "environment", "role": "place, weather, time of day"},
    {"id": "camera", "role": "shot size, angle, one primary move — own sentence"},
    {"id": "lighting", "role": "source, direction, quality"},
    {"id": "style", "role": "medium and grade; Xochipilli sends this as STYLE LOCK"},
    {"id": "audio", "role": "providers with native audio; this pipeline strips it (-an)"}
  ],
  "rules": [
    "One primary camera move per clip. Two conflicting moves produce drift.",
    "Put the camera move in its own sentence, not buried in scene description.",
    "Write what should happen, not what should not. Negation inside the positive prompt is unreliable; exclusions belong in the AVOID / NEGATIVE block.",
    "To hold a frame still, describe stillness positively (locked-off tripod, only the subject animates) — that is what CAMERA_LOCK_TEXT does.",
    "Seed, resolution, frame rate and duration are call parameters, not prompt text. This pipeline re-encodes every part to 1280x720@24.",
    "A clip here is about 5 seconds. Describe one beat, not a narrative.",
    "For continuity across takes, a reference still (i2v / extension) beats seed matching."
  ],
  "terms": [
